wundefined-42\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-guruṇā\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=guruṇā\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"guruṇā\"}]}],\" \",[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-2-api\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=api\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"api\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"even though very difficult\"}}],\"; \"]}]\n52:[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-43\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-vicālyate\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=vicālyate\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"vicālyate\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"becomes shaken\"}}],\"; \"]}]\n53:[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-44\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-tam\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=tam\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"tam\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"that\"}}],\"; \"]}]\n54:[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-45\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-vidyāt\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=vidyāt\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"vidyāt\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"you must know\"}}],\"; \"]}]\n55:[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-46\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-duḥkha\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=duḥkha\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"duḥkha\"}]}],\"-\",[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-2-saṁyoga\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=saṁyoga\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"saṁyoga\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"of the miseries of material contact\"}}],\"; \"]}]\n56:[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-47\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-viyogam\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=viyogam\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"viyogam\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"extermination\"}}],\"; \"]}]\n57:[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-48\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-yoga\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=yoga\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"yoga\"}]}],\"-\",[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-2-saṁjñitam\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=saṁjñitam\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"saṁjñitam\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"called trance in yoga.\"}}],\".\"]}]\n5d:T51a,In the yoga system, as described in this chapter, there are two kinds of samādhi, called samprajñāta-samādhi and asamprajñāta-samādhi. When one becomes situated in the transcendental position by various philosophical researches, he is said to have achieved samprajñāta-samādhi. In the asamprajñāta-samādhi there is no longer any connection with mundane pleasure, for one is then transcendental to all sorts of happiness derived from the senses. When the yogī is once situated in that transcendental position, he is never shaken from it. Unless the yogī is able to reach this position, "])self.__next_f.push([1,"he is unsuccessful. Today’s so-called yoga practice, which involves various sense pleasures, is contradictory. A yogī indulging in sex and intoxication is a mockery. Even those yogīs who are attracted by the siddhis (perfections) in the process of yoga are not perfectly situated. If yogīs are attracted by the by-products of yoga, then they cannot attain the stage of perfection, as is stated in this verse. Persons, therefore, indulging in the make-show practice of gymnastic feats or siddhis should know that the aim of yoga is lost in that way.59:[\"$\",\"$L2c\",\"child-1896\",{\"child\":\"$23:props:children:0:props:children:props:page:child_items:4:children:3\",\"hasId\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"em-mb-4 em-leading-8 em-text-base s-justify\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$5d\"}}]}]\n5a:[\"$\",\"$L2c\",\"child-1897\",{\"child\":\"$23:props:children:0:props:children:props:page:child_items:4:children:4\",\"hasId\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"em-mb-4 em-leading-8 em-text-base s-justify\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"The best practice of yoga in this age is Kṛṣṇa consciousness, which is not baffling. A Kṛṣṇa conscious person is so happy in his occupation that he does not aspire after any other happiness. There are many impediments, especially in this age of hypocrisy, to practicing haṭha-yoga, dhyāna-yoga and jñāna-yoga, but there is no such problem in executing karma-yoga or bhakti-yoga.\"}}]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"5b:[\"$\",\"$L2c\",\"child-1898\",{\"child\":\"$23:props:children:0:props:children:props:page:child_items:4:children:5\",\"hasId\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"em-mb-4 em-leading-8 em-text-base s-justify\",\"children\":[\"As long as the material body exists, one has to meet the demands of the body, namely eating, sleeping, defending and mating. But a person who is in pure \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"1\",{\"children\":\"bhakti-yoga,\"}],\" or in Kṛṣṇa consciousness, does not arouse the senses while meeting the demands of the body. Rather, he accepts the bare necessities of life, making the best use of a bad bargain, and enjoys transcendental happiness in Kṛṣṇa consciousness. He is callous toward incidental occurrences – such as accidents, disease, scarcity and even the death of a most dear relative – but he is always alert to execute his duties in Kṛṣṇa consciousness, or \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"3\",{\"children\":\"bhakti-yoga.\"}],\" Accidents never deviate him from his duty. As stated in the \",[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"5\",{\"href\":\"/en/library/bg/2/14/\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"em\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"Bhagavad-gītā\"}],\" (2.14)\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"7\",{\"children\":\"āgamāpāyino ’nityās tāṁs titikṣasva bhārata.\"}],\" He endures all such incidental occurrences because he knows that they come and go and do not affect his duties. In this way he achieves the highest perfection in \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"9\",{\"children\":\"yoga\"}],\" practice.\"]}]}]\n"])(function(){function c(){var b=a.contentDocument||(a.contentWindow&&a.contentWindow.document);if(b){var d=b.createElement(''script'');d.innerHTML="window.__CF$cv$params={r:''a340570ccbb5f501'',t:''MTc4ODIyNDQ0Nw==''};var a=document.createElement(''script'');a.src=''/cdn-cgi/challenge-platform/scripts/jsd/main.js'';document.getElementsByTagName(''head'')[0].appendChild(a);";b.getElementsByTagName(''head'')[0].appendChild(d)}}if(document.body){var a=document.createElement(''iframe'');a.height=1;a.width=1;a.style.position=''absolute'';a.style.top=0;a.style.left=0;a.style.border=''none'';a.style.visibility=''hidden'';document.body.appendChild(a);if(''loading''!==document.readyState)c();else if(window.addEventListener)document.addEventListener(''DOMContentLoaded'',c);else{var e=document.onreadystatechange||function(){};document.onreadystatechange=function(b){e(b);''loading''!==document.readyState&&(document.onreadystatechange=e,c())}}}})();', 'https://vedabase.io/en/library/bg/6/20-23/', true)
